{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Lazy Initialization.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Lazy Initialization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"lazy initialization lazy initialization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Lazy Initialization.md","fileName":"Lazy Initialization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Lazy Initialization","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 00:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[.NET Concurrent Collections and Lazy Initialization]]","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Concurrent Collections and Lazy Initialization","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Lazy Initialization.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Lazy Initialization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"lazy initialization lazy initialization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Lazy Initialization.md","fileName":"Lazy Initialization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Lazy Initialization","heading":"Lazy Initialization","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Lazy initialization postpones creating a value until the program first needs it. Deferral can reduce startup time, memory use, and wasted computation when an expensive object is never accessed.\n\nIn concurrent code, the first-access path must prevent duplicate or partially published construction unless the design explicitly permits it. The cost of synchronization and the consequences of construction failure should be weighed against the resource savings of deferral.","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Concurrent Collections and Lazy Initialization","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Lazy Initialization.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Lazy Initialization.md","sourceType":"markd